-- title:
--   Canonical full slow rows converge relatively to reference rows
-- statement:
--   For every r>0 there is W₀ such that W≥W₀ can be fixed before the relative mesh, head patterns, physical intervals, ledger and tilt bounds. Here a canonical bridge means the guarded canonical sample at the indicated n and W, with separated physical intervals, a nonempty remainder in each cell, and the canonical mesh prime partition. The finite nonempty head family has exactly the primes at most W in each head pattern. Physical interval endpoints lie between 1 and a fixed upper bound; guard ledgers have fixed promotion and bank parameters. Assume δ>0, w=δ+η, and nonnegative bounds Acoef,Aphys on the effective prime coefficients and physical tilt coordinate. Eventually in n, uniformly over canonical bridges and allowed ξ, the full-valuation slow row obeys the following estimate in every band. This strengthens squarefree approximation to the actual valuation law.
--
--   $$|R_{\rm full}(\xi,i)-R_{\rm ref}(i)|\le r w\alpha_i.$$
